WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.150
We have a voicemail number.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.220
That number is two.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:10.990
One nine two, David P, uh, yesterday I talked
about the cult like nature of Trumpists, both

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:17.020
a cult of personality around Trump, but also
the very cult like behavior of many of Trump's

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:24.190
followers, which includes, um, uh, always
finding reasons why the bad things that Trump

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.390
does aren't really bad.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.820
Ignoring information about bad things that
Donald Trump does.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.390
We talked about it all before.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:37.960
I got a voicemail yesterday from a Trumpist
who says he is not pleased with me making

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.399
the cultist analogy.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:40.429
Take a listen to this.

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:41.429
Yeah.

00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:42.750
Just watch your show.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:50.820
Will you, um, lambasted, uh, Tucker Carlson
and I'm a Trump supporter and there are 62

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:59.140
million of us, or 60 million of us, and you're
really condescending and insulting to us that

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:06.960
we're not smart enough to think on her own
or how we're gonna pay for something.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.140
I'm, I mean, it's ridiculous the way you talk
about us, that we're a cult.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.979
Are you kidding me?

00:01:15.979 --> 00:01:18.170
No one's going to put me in a Colt.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.969
No politician is going to brainwash me into
voting for them.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:23.969
Yeah.

00:01:23.969 --> 00:01:27.939
I mean, you know, one of the things that's
important to understand about cults is nobody

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:33.509
who's in a cult thinks they're in a cult until
sometimes after they've left the cult.

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:37.329
No one who is brainwashed believes that they
have been brainwashed.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:41.409
Because knowing you've been brainwashed would
be an antidote to the brainwashing.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:46.630
And the reality is a lot of people who voted
for Trump are ignorant people.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.250
I, I've said before, there's ignorant people
on all sides of the political spectrum.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.080
If someone in an uninformed way votes for
a Democrat or a progressive or whatever, it's

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.869
not any less informed than an ignorant Republican
voter.

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:01.159
I would be glad if they end up making the
right decision.

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:03.229
But there's uninformed and ignorant voters
on both sides.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:07.469
But as I said before, there are basically
three categories of people who voted for Donald

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:08.469
Trump.

00:02:08.469 --> 00:02:10.750
And I know this pisses a lot of people off
there.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.050
Ignorant people, right?

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:15.220
People who just didn't know what they were
voting for, they didn't understand they were,

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:18.810
they either fell for things Trump said that
were impossible and said, this is why I'm

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.970
gonna vote for the guy without realizing that
the, the, the, the, the, they were impossible

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.210
promises or they just don't pay attention
to the politics.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.120
Ignorance to some degree.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.480
There are people who are cognitively limited
and that, again, I'm not insulting anybody,

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.060
it's just there's a lot of people in, in the
electorate who vote, but they don't really

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:40.310
have the cognitive capacity to understand
what is going on.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.569
It's not ignorance, but it's a limitation.

00:02:42.569 --> 00:02:48.360
And then you have just what I would call bad
people and I know that good, bad is, it's

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.400
a very rudimentary and unsophisticated way
to categorize.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.209
But what I mean by bad people is it's not
people who are cognitively limited.

00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:57.220
It's not people who are ignorant to the facts.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.970
It's people who understand exactly what it
is that Donald Trump is promising and they

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.189
like it, right?

00:03:03.189 --> 00:03:07.550
They like it because it's good for them personally
because of taxes, for example, or whatever.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.129
Those are the three categories.

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:14.780
I've still not met anyone to this day who
voted for Trump, who doesn't fall into one

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.989
of those three categories and I will completely
concede to you that there are people on the

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:23.580
left, at least with two of those three categories
that we could identify as well.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:24.580
Prove me wrong.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.090
I'm open to having my mind changed.

